# Everything the image must NOT receive.
#
# Two reasons this file matters more than usual here:
#   1. venv/ is a Windows virtualenv — hundreds of MB of .exe/.pyd that
#      are useless and unloadable on Linux. Without this line every
#      `docker build` uploads it as build context.
#   2. .env holds the OpenAI key, the SMTP password and the DB password.
#      It is deliberately NOT copied into the image; docker compose
#      injects the values at run time from .env.docker instead, so the
#      secrets never end up in an image layer.

# --- virtualenvs (Windows-built, unusable in Linux) ---
venv/
.venv/
env/

# --- python bytecode / caches ---
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- previous Nuitka output (regenerated every build) ---
build/
dist/
*.so
*.pyi

# --- runtime data, mounted as volumes instead ---
logs/
uploads/
backups/

# --- secrets: injected via docker compose env_file, never baked in ---
.env
.env.*

# --- not needed to build or run the API ---
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
tests/
scripts/
*.md
README
